#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083054 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "15c029df-b002-51cc-87db-a94d40a02771" :question/math-academy-id "e-595" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\cos{t}, \\quad y=\\sin{t}, \\qquad  0\\leq t<2\\pi,\n$$\n\n calculate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$\n\n![](images/2e/2ec95dd061fa6b7f09c9f899a1f6483b4ea7d5127372ddd6eefb74d6ed10c14c.png)" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = -\\sin{t}, \\qquad y'(t)=\\cos{t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\cos t}{-\\sin t} = -\\cot t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083055 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "148e5378-9177-59ba-9b1e-3633c940babd" :question/math-academy-id "e-596" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=te^t, \\quad y=e^{-t}, \\qquad -\\infty < t <\\infty,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = e^t + te^t = (1+t)e^t, \\qquad y'(t)=-e^{-t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-{e}^{-t}}{(1+t){e}^{t}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(1+t){e}^{2t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t=1} & =-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2(1)}(1+1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18fb0b4b-0bf1-5c76-8696-c067c4ad8969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272604} {:answer/id #uuid "6347253c-9fd4-5926-94fe-94155ab5318b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273242} {:answer/id #uuid "722f7007-9e15-5b79-bcc7-366580ece601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273367} {:answer/id #uuid "880d64e6-f8cb-55ff-8d8e-f7e554ac9ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273554} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9c124b-193b-5381-9981-884d4b7bd866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "722f7007-9e15-5b79-bcc7-366580ece601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273367} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5e582ec-54ef-57eb-ade9-5e1ede765e24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d08529b-8573-5553-9a9b-ff64d66c71ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-15457" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,y={cos}^{2}⁡(t),\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b6edb1b-f7b7-5718-8cda-0dd5a71a50be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272774} {:answer/id #uuid "2d253935-f522-5f06-9ee4-61b8bb0a1972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272789} {:answer/id #uuid "2e13d3fc-0795-5608-98ad-09cff47ca45a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272799} {:answer/id #uuid "6a2e7d1f-a9f1-5d66-a415-8d8c4115d124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273303} {:answer/id #uuid "de45196d-d0c1-55a1-8019-f950885e3562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b6edb1b-f7b7-5718-8cda-0dd5a71a50be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272774} :answer-field/id #uuid "f570cb94-97be-59e0-a398-fb3eb82d9321" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "18a41cc2-6786-5c7c-b54f-7a6c8dbb881f" :question/math-academy-id "q-15476" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t})},\\,y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡({e}^{t}),\\,-\\infty <t<1,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t})}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t})\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t})}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t})}}, \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) & =-{e}^{t}{csc}^{2}⁡({e}^{t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-{e}^{t}{csc}^{2}⁡({e}^{t})}{(\\frac{{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t})}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t})}})} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t})}}{{sin}^{2}⁡({e}^{t})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t})} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{2}{{sin}^{3/2}⁡({e}^{t})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t})}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{2}{{sin}^{3/2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{2}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3/2}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {2}^{3/2}\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =-8\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3b7074a-75b7-5dfa-ba96-9067b0b0c2da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403274} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca59391-4b16-5de2-b31a-e434042882de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{2e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403275} {:answer/id #uuid "b7da2d97-ee19-5b91-aae1-d3e1ef8e41cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403276} {:answer/id #uuid "c0595185-9dbe-5e61-833d-f322b3bc5d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403277} {:answer/id #uuid "efa241d0-aa74-5ee0-84e5-879e44d2f438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{3e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0595185-9dbe-5e61-833d-f322b3bc5d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403277} :answer-field/id #uuid "cade3433-2a7c-573e-ae14-9f4f0ad1cbde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef78af33-68fa-5c96-9f7c-05772b13cffb" :question/math-academy-id "q-6812" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=({t}^{3}-1){e}^{t},\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=({t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1){e}^{t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{({t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1){e}^{t}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=0$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{({0}^{3}+3\\cdot {0}^{2}-1){e}^{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1)}{(-1)\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5acc6cd8-f001-5394-a6fb-c1dd0fc5b3b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333819} {:answer/id #uuid "911bd715-c47b-52fc-8b17-1d94b494a8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334283} {:answer/id #uuid "a6a0b785-553c-5b96-8cde-3a695db73d7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334450} {:answer/id #uuid "aef4e7d5-b6bf-5eef-a5a0-2697f1745f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334529} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b6f7ec-a4b3-53d6-a622-e814425b78ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aef4e7d5-b6bf-5eef-a5a0-2697f1745f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334529} :answer-field/id #uuid "b356f94f-948d-5358-9ef9-3fb6cfeb2cdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18b27deb-1f86-5103-a5ac-bd0f135dadc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-6816" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{2t},\\,y=({t}^{2}-1){e}^{-t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{e}^{2t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}}{2{e}^{2t}}=\\frac{1}{2}(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-3t}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2(1)-(1)^{2}){e}^{-3(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2-1){e}^{-3} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
